  "description": "Cross-process synchronization for Compze.Threading. A system-mutex-backed IAwaitableMutex that offers the full Monitor.Wait condition-wait model across process boundaries, plus IProcessShared/IAwaitableProcessShared, the file-based InterprocessSignal, IProcessLock, a lock between processes that any thread can release and the operating system releases when its holder dies, IProcessSemaphore, a counting semaphore between processes that serves takes in the order they came and that a dead holder can't leave held, and IInterprocessObject, an object shared between processes, created in a single line of code, with atomic updates, waits for conditions to become true, recovery from corruption and pluggable serialization. Extracted from Compze.Threading 0.7.0-alpha; IInterprocessObject moved here from the retired Compze.InterprocessObject.",
